                <pb facs="0845" n="1679" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1679"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/817</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-03T22:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 3, 1918, 10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 5, 5.20 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1298. Embassy’s 1293, May 3, 9 p.m., War Trade Board 44 from Chadbourne. Embassy
                    cannot support recommendations therein contained. While terms of
                    Spanish-American agreement of March 7, 1918, have been technically violated in
                    delay and otherwise by Spanish Government, yet United States Government is
                    securing and accepting practically all the agreement calls for. Therefore to
                    notify Spanish Government that agreement is at end is serious step and one to be
                    taken only after great consideration and consultation with French Government
                    which is indirect party to contract. Moreover such action would bring about
                    immediate withdrawal of French credit. This question also involves political
                    policy and good faith. Embassy requests instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
